<title>MEXICO: Banco de Mexico assigns all secondary auctions.</title>
<headline>Banco de Mexico assigns all secondary auctions.</headline>
<dateline>MEXICO CITY 1997-03-11</dateline>
<text>
<p>Banco de Mexico assigned all seven auctions it had offered in order to drain 5.797 billion pesos from the secondary market on Tuesday, dealers said.</p>
<p>The auctions were assigned as follows:</p>
<p>    AMOUNT     TERM     AVERAGE RATE</p>
<p>600 million  31 days  25.49 pct</p>
<p>600 million  30 days  25.40 pct</p>
<p>600 million  27 days  25.48 pct</p>
<p>1.400 bln  20 days  25.47 pct</p>
<p>1.300 bln   9 days  25.67 pct</p>
<p>600 million   3 days  25.80 pct</p>
<p>697 million   1 day   24.87 pct</p>
<p>*Amounts in pesos</p>
<p>((-- Mexico City newsroom 525 728-9559))</p>
</text>
